- All right, because, all right.

00:34:23.230 --> 00:34:27.470
So the reason, y'all
have seen this before.

00:34:27.470 --> 00:34:29.050
The reason why this I think went viral

00:34:29.050 --> 00:34:31.750
is some people, you know
you learn in school,

00:34:31.750 --> 00:34:34.130
order of operations, some
people learn things like PEMDAS,

00:34:34.130 --> 00:34:34.963
which is like

00:34:34.963 --> 00:34:36.880
parentheses, exponents,
multiplication, division,

00:34:36.880 --> 00:34:38.500
addition, subtraction.

00:34:38.500 --> 00:34:41.220
You often times learned in school,

00:34:41.220 --> 00:34:43.340
you do parenthesis first, that's obvious,

00:34:43.340 --> 00:34:48.340
but then multiplication and
division are kind of equal

00:34:48.380 --> 00:34:50.490
and when in doubt you
do them left to right

00:34:50.490 --> 00:34:52.420
and then addition and
subtraction are kind of equal

00:34:52.420 --> 00:34:54.630
and when in doubt do them left to right.

00:34:54.630 --> 00:34:56.710
What's tricky here is,
okay so the obvious part

00:34:56.710 --> 00:34:57.740
is to do the parenthesis first,

00:34:57.740 --> 00:34:59.210
I don't think anyone debates that.

00:34:59.210 --> 00:35:01.380
So that's just four right there.

00:35:01.380 --> 00:35:04.273
So you have eight divided
by two times four.

00:35:05.200 --> 00:35:08.550
Now if you take the left
to right attitude about it,

00:35:08.550 --> 00:35:13.550
you'd say eight divided
by two is four times four

00:35:13.800 --> 00:35:17.290
which is 16, that's one
way people have done it.

00:35:17.290 --> 00:35:18.247
The other way people have said is,

00:35:18.247 --> 00:35:21.527
"Wait, but if I see a number
right next to the parenthesis,

00:35:21.527 --> 00:35:23.847
"I feel like I have to
multiply that first."

00:35:23.847 --> 00:35:24.680
- Right.

00:35:24.680 --> 00:35:27.050
- So people say two
times four that's eight,

00:35:27.050 --> 00:35:29.100
and then eight divided
by eight would be one,

00:35:29.100 --> 00:35:31.640
so you get either 16 or one.

00:35:31.640 --> 00:35:33.427
I think, maybe other
people got other things

00:35:33.427 --> 00:35:35.850
but that might a little
bit more suspicious.

00:35:35.850 --> 00:35:38.510
My take on it, I mean one,
this tells you why you learn

00:35:38.510 --> 00:35:39.870
something like order of operations.

00:35:39.870 --> 00:35:42.200
Order of operations are just
to try to remove ambiguity

00:35:42.200 --> 00:35:44.483
from mathematical expressions like this.

00:35:45.700 --> 00:35:48.330
My view on this is.

00:35:48.330 --> 00:35:51.140
If I see a number right
next to parenthesis,

00:35:51.140 --> 00:35:54.920
I almost view that as like
a light form of parenthesis,

00:35:54.920 --> 00:35:57.140
a light form of emphasis of like,

00:35:57.140 --> 00:36:00.730
you're going to do that,
you're going to do that first.

00:36:00.730 --> 00:36:05.110
So I would, my inclination
would be to go to the one.

00:36:05.110 --> 00:36:08.260
Eight divided by two times
four, so eight divided eight

00:36:08.260 --> 00:36:09.690
which is one.

00:36:09.690 --> 00:36:11.460
But, this is why if you're doing it,

00:36:11.460 --> 00:36:13.490
look, even if you're doing a maths thesis,

00:36:13.490 --> 00:36:15.440
this is why it's good to
even use more parenthesis,

00:36:15.440 --> 00:36:17.060
when in doubt use extra parenthesis,

00:36:17.060 --> 00:36:19.810
if you think what you're
saying can be ambiguous.

00:36:19.810 --> 00:36:21.090
In fact, that's not true just in math,

00:36:21.090 --> 00:36:24.300
that's true in life especially
if it's something important,

00:36:24.300 --> 00:36:26.630
explain it, be very clear.

00:36:26.630 --> 00:36:29.000
But you know, these are just symbols

00:36:29.000 --> 00:36:30.990
that are trying to convey an idea

00:36:30.990 --> 00:36:32.640
and you don't want to be ambiguous

00:36:32.640 --> 00:36:34.590
and so if you think it's
going to be ambiguous

00:36:34.590 --> 00:36:35.980
just put another parenthesis around that.

00:36:35.980 --> 00:36:37.730
Or if you really wanted
the eight to be divided

00:36:37.730 --> 00:36:39.940
by two before you multiply,
then put the parenthesis

00:36:39.940 --> 00:36:41.110
around that first.

00:36:41.110 --> 00:36:43.500
So I would say whoever
did this just should've

00:36:43.500 --> 00:36:45.220
included more parenthesis,
but my inclination

00:36:45.220 --> 00:36:48.540
is definitely to do the two
times the parenthesis first

00:36:48.540 --> 00:36:49.770
'cause it's right next to it.

00:36:49.770 --> 00:36:52.420
If there's a multiplication symbol there

00:36:52.420 --> 00:36:55.440
then I probably would've
gone left to right,

00:36:55.440 --> 00:36:56.320
hopefully that's helpful.

